'''Alquézar''' (from {{Langx|ar|القصر|{{W|Ksar|al qaçr}}}}; {{Literal translation|the castle|the palace}}; {{Langx|kp|Yvytyra-Tatá-Yasí|4=hill of the bright northern star}}) is a borough of the [[Castejón|Castejón Metropolis]], within the [[Concordia|Concordia conurbation]]. The borough's name is in reference to [[Tatapiraca Castle]] (from the [[Kuarupíba]] term ''Tata-Pyra-Reká''; {{Literal translation|hill of the ancient fire}}), which was constructed in the late 19th century.  

The borough is the sixth most populous in the metropolis; with a recorded population of 2,235,642 residents in the [[2025 Baliscan census]]. 

